  "body": "**Describe the bug**\nRollingUpdate of workspace deployment is not working as expected. Upon deployment of workspace with fine tuned adapters, existing workspace pod is terminated immediately before the new workspace pod is up and running. New pod takes around 5-10 mins for pulling adapter and be in ready state. This leads to downtime in service.\n\n**Steps To Reproduce**\nDeploy workspace with single adapter first, once pod is ready. Update workspace and add another adapter and deploy modified workspace, old pod will be terminated immediately and new pod will take 5-10 mins to be up and running.\n\n**Expected behavior**\nExisting pod should keep on running until new pod is in running state.\n\n\n**Additional context**\nValue of maxsurge should be 1 and maxavailable should be 0\nhttps://github.com/kaito-project/kaito/blob/140a5f97f24be9f20c1490f7bc6860731f0b7098/pkg/workspace/manifests/manifests.go#L267\n\nOr expose these so users can set these as needed\nCurrently, there is no mechanism to override these values via function parameters or workspace object fields. They are not exposed as configurable options in the function signature or through the workspace spec\u2014the values are set in code.",
